This repository contains the standalone ComfyUI node implementation.
It integrates the Krea2 SingleStreamDiT and LoRA bypass APIs provided by
ComfyUI (https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI).
The compiled block wrapper follows the upstream Krea2 block's mathematical
sequence; the native model and adapter calculations remain upstream code.
ComfyUI and its contributors retain their respective copyrights.

The Q/K GEMM visitor in kernels/qk_norm_rope.cu adapts the NVIDIA CUTLASS
VisitorAuxStore callback structure (BSD-3-Clause). Copyright (c) 2017 - 2026
NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. The original license is reproduced in
third_party/CUTLASS-LICENSE.txt. CUTLASS headers and binaries remain external
dependencies. The RMS reduction ordering follows PyTorch ATen 2.9's CUDA
RMSNorm implementation (https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch).

The normalized-input INT4 quantizer in kernels/norm_quant.cu reuses and adapts
ComfyKitchen's ConvRot transform and packing sequence (Apache-2.0), revision
255a43879fe57bbcbecfdb273b46d772b00c5a90. Copyright (c) 2025 Comfy Org.
Its build script extracts the original device helper prefix without modification
and adds explicitly rounded RMSNorm/modulation ahead of that sequence. The
license and upstream notice are in third_party/comfy-kitchen/.

KohakuKernelRouter adapts the shape bucketing, CUDA-event timing, per-kernel
winner tables and fused/split binding flow from KohakuMossTrainer, revision
0536e62b6062039104d8f9575635b5d07bf573d3:
https://github.com/KohakuBlueleaf/KohakuMossTrainer
Original files: src/kohakumoss_kernels/tuning/{timing,tuner,buckets}.py and
src/kohakumoss_kernels/backends/triton/attention/{_kernels,varlen}.py.
The FA forward is adapted for direct GQA head indexing, strided batched inputs,
optional masks and gated inference output; no K/V head replication is performed.
